# GML8W: Run llama-cpp gguf LLM model

This document shows how to run LLM model in GGUF format with llama-cpp backend engine

---

### 1. Model ID

Find model id by listing all available model entry by invoking `gml8w --help`

- Format of model entry: `<MODEL_ID>:<MODEL_NAME>: ["<MODEL_DESCRIPTION>", "<LLAMACPP_PARAMS>"]`

- Example: `4` is MODEL_ID, `gemma-4-e4b-it-Q4_K_M.gguf` is model name, `Agent8083` is model descript, `--port 8083` is one of llama-cpp params
  
  ```
  4:lmstudio-community/gemma-4-E4B-it-GGUF/gemma-4-e4b-it-Q4_K_M.gguf: ["Agent8083" , "-b 4096 -ub 4096 -c 8192 -ctk q4_0 -ctv q4_0 -fa on -nkvo --port 8083 --embeddings --pooling mean"]
  ```

### 2. Run Commands

| Command            | Description                               | Example        |
| ------------------ | ----------------------------------------- | -------------- |
| `gml8w --help`     | List all available LLM models             | `gml8w --help` |
| `gml8w <MODEL_ID>` | Run LLM model by specific ID (using `wt`) | `gml8w 4`      |

### 3. Instructions

1. Find `<MODEL_ID>` using `gml8w --help` command

2. Run command `gml8w <MODEL_ID>` in background using `wt` command
   Example: `wt  "C:\Program Files\Git\bin\bash.exe" -li -c "gml8w 4"`

3. Test if command launched successfully:
   `curl  http://localhost:<PORT>/v1/models`


